ios: action label

On a touch screen nothing hovers and the finger covers what it taps, so the hover text (drawFeedback, shown only
while a finger is down) flashes by on a tap and the red cross alone does not say what the tap did. doAction now
wraps the upstream handler (doMenuAction): after an action that starts a red cross (an op on an NPC, player, loc or
ground item, an item used or a spell cast on one, also from the long-press menu) or acts on an item in a slot (an
inventory, worn equipment, the bank, a shop: OP_HELD1-6, TGT_HELD, USEHELD_START/ONHELD, INV_BUTTON1-5) it tells the
host: lcEvent 'action-label' { text: the option as drawn, colour tags included, x, y: the red cross or the tapped
point in page px }. The host shows it beside that point (menu.js). GameShell.pagePoint maps a virtual point to the
page through the surface (or the canvas) that shows it, the inverse of getMousePos. Touch screens only.

